    {
      "id": "848dfeb47274ef0efc41434c34003c22eb62a665",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 917328261,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "!6748 fixes #18043 by allowing NULL to be passed to conversation_get_proto_data. If we merge that, would the additional \"conv\" checks here improve dissection?",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789887783",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-19T20:39:33.695Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-20T06:52:13.646Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 151128913,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789887783",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-04-21T16:27:34.961Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 6755,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 917668068,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I'm totally with you. However in the past other core devels have criticized this kind of defensive approach, stating that it is meaningless that a dissector asks something using a null pointer. That's clearly a mistake, then how would we want to approach it?\n\n1. the dissector must check. A wrong call it's their mistake (this change)\n2. the called should check. A wrong call fails silently (change !6748)\n3. the called should check. A wrong call triggers an exception (TODO)\n\nWith (1) we fix a dissectors, but others need fixing. With (2) we fix everything, but invalid code paths that lead to null pointers passing will fail silently. With (3) we will notice where problems are, but the dissectors still need fixing.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-20T06:52:13.585Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-20T06:52:13.585Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 151128913,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789887783",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-04-21T16:27:34.961Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 6755,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 918720675,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I understand the concern about the meaningless behavior, but I have a concern about having to request a CVE any time a dissector in a release branch exhibits this behavior. I'll try to update !6748 to call report_dissector_bug, which would give us option 3.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789887783",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-20T18:21:17.213Z",
